settings: fix get_axis_mask() signature

get_axis_mask() is stored as a setting getter and called through
setting_get_int_ptr, which takes a single setting_id_t. The extra unused
int_value parameter is harmless on ARM but traps in WebAssembly, where an
indirect call must match the callee signature exactly.

diff --git a/settings.c b/settings.c
index c2f3370..f979dfe 100644
--- a/settings.c
+++ b/settings.c
@@ -706,7 +706,7 @@ FLASHMEM static status_code_t set_axis_mask (setting_id_t id, uint_fast16_t valu
     return status;
 }
 
-FLASHMEM static uint32_t get_axis_mask (setting_id_t id, uint_fast16_t int_value)
+FLASHMEM static uint32_t get_axis_mask (setting_id_t id)
 {
     uint32_t value = 0;
 
